Z||000000||FieroJoe||04-29-2001||12:03 AM||||I have removed my stamped louver sheet from my engine vents (have noticed a differnece in temp of air coming out), and I am ok with having the vapor canistor exposed, but I'd really like something that I could cover up my battery with.  I'd rather not show off my battery to anyone who walks by.  I was thinking of some sort cover I could put over the top of the battery and the terminals.<P>Anybody done something like this, or have any suggestions?  The only thing I could come up with would be bending plexiglass and then painting it black.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FieroJoe87<BR>87 Coupe 5spd<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||04-29-2001||12:13 AM||||Hey Joe!<BR>If you go to your local plexiglas outlet, you will find it comes in many colors...<BR>You can buy the materials to make a very nice box type of cover, and the nice part, it won't rust...<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||jaguiler||04-29-2001||09:13 AM||||go to a marine supply store and they have covered waterproof boxes to fit boat batteries....<P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
